  'guides.user.add-mcp.title': 'Connect an external tool (MCP server)',
  'guides.user.add-mcp.sub': 'Attach an MCP server so your AI Agent can use tools from another system.',
  'guides.user.add-mcp.what': 'An MCP server lets the AI Agent use features of another system (for example, a calendar, an issue tracker or a company database). Once connected, that system\'s features become tools the AI Agent can use. A connected server acts with the permissions of the key you entered. When someone else asks this AI Agent for work in the office or a meeting room, it uses the same permissions.',
  'guides.user.add-mcp.when': 'Use it when you want the AI Agent to read or work with data in a company system. Get the server address or command from the person who runs that system.',
  'guides.user.add-mcp.open.title': 'Open the {p_tools} tab',
  'guides.user.add-mcp.open.body': 'Open the "{p_tools}" tab of your main profile. Connected servers are listed under "MCP servers".',
  'guides.user.add-mcp.add.title': 'Add a server',
  'guides.user.add-mcp.add.body': 'Click Add server and choose how to add it. The dialog opens on Catalog, a prepared list. Choose Remote address if you received a server address, or Run a program if you received a command. For a Docmost wiki, pick "docmost" in the catalog and enter the MCP address and your own key created in Docmost Settings > API keys. Read tools are registered by default; choose "Also register write tools" to write pages and comments too. This profile\'s browser and connections tools are turned off and the usage-rules skill (docmost) is installed with it. For an Outline wiki, pick "outline" in the catalog and enter the MCP address and your own key created in Outline Settings > API. To read only, enter read in Scopes when you create the key. Delete tools are not registered even with write tools. This profile\'s browser and connections tools are turned off and the usage-rules skill (outline) is installed with it. If you remove the Outline server later, those two stay off; turn them on in the Tools tab if you need them. After you change the write tools switch, click Apply now. After connecting, use it in a new chat. When you save and the dialog closes, click Next on the card.',
  'guides.user.add-mcp.test.title': 'Test the connection',
  'guides.user.add-mcp.test.body': 'Click "Test connection" on the server row to see the number of tools. If it fails, follow the error message.',

  'guides.user.secret.title': 'Add a secret such as an API key',
